}(T)?$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $u$ belongs to the kernel of a linear transformation $T$ if $T(u)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, we need to compute $T({v}_{i})$ for each ${v}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\,T({v}_{i})\\ne 0$ for any $i$'s, we conclude that none of them belongs to the kernel of $\\,T.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af17e52-688b-5b75-8902-65be7464d50b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-139998/selection/6915ee1686a56fd229eba5fad60cd3b821ac3a8bdd716a82581fe6b91ea9a7c3" :answer/id #uuid "b0e6228f-1e47-5ff6-82ff-83097aae3f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$  and ${v}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139998/selection/95bc21f42086862d75a0cc3c5d4cafd4f1bd6c7cc83a994eb3f5926dc6b486dc" :answer/id #uuid "57e003d1-c268-5a77-9265-f64e72016ff9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139998/selection/156be9b9cf165ab878e6945158eb69b6d92f28ff22d964498ac0fd056dd5221f" :answer/id #uuid "7fc770bf-0581-5b4b-849f-9ed418837d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$  and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139998/selection/58b5e179955bf0f386c3edca2bc3f6ba9a4f2d6467c1e5972f26adcd58b9f00c" :answer/id #uuid "f8886185-ef1f-5f17-8bdc-4d2143b80373" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$  and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13